WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.760
Every carbon atom in a plant was
once carbon dioxide in the air.

2
00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:09.450
Each one was built into sugar by a
cycle of reactions in the chloroplast:

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.060
the Calvin cycle.

4
00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.970
That cycle uses no light directly.

5
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:17.060
Yet switch off the
lamp, and it soon stops.

6
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:21.670
So if this stage needs no light,
why does it stop in the dark?

7
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.670
In this mission, you'll
see where the cycle runs:

8
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.160
in the stroma, the fluid
around the thylakoids.

9
00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:32.860
Then you'll work out what happens
inside a leaf once the light goes out.

10
00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:36.950
Your mission: explain why the leaf
stops making sugar in the dark,

11
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.080
though this stage needs no light.
